1. default is unsorted (selection order): select<count=2>(text="alpha beta gamma delta")
2. sorted=true restores original text order: select<count=2,sorted=true>(text="alpha beta gamma delta")
3. a bare sorted flag means sorted=true: select<count=2,sorted>(text="alpha beta gamma delta")
4. a count above the item count implies dups: select<count=6>(text="a b c")
5. explicit dups=true allows repeats: select<count=3,dups=true,sorted=true>(text="a b c d e")
6. a bare dups flag also allows repeats: select<count=3,dups,sorted>(text="a b c d e")
7. dups=false (default) never repeats when count fits: select<count=3,sorted=true>(text="a b c d e")
8. an invalid bool value warns and falls back to the default: select<count=2,sorted=maybe>(text="a b c d")
9. a plain bare word is still a positional value, not a flag: show(hello)
